{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "label": "codebase-design (deep-module vocabulary)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A language, not a procedure - fixes the words (module, interface, depth, seam, adapter, leverage, locality) so design conversations speak the same way. Component, service, API, and boundary are deliberately banned for blurring distinctions."}, {"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_deep_module", "label": "Deep module", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A large amount of behaviour behind a small interface; depth is measured as leverage - how much a caller or test can exercise per unit of interface learned. Depth is a property of the interface, not the implementation."}, {"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_seam", "label": "Seam", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Feathers' term - a place you can change behaviour without editing there; preferred over the overloaded boundary. Callers and tests cross the same seam, so the interface is the test surface. Interface means every fact a caller must know: signatures, invariants, ordering, error modes, performance."}, {"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_deletion_test", "label": "Deletion test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Imagine deleting the module - if complexity vanishes it was a pass-through; if it reappears across N callers it was earning its keep."}, {"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_two_adapters_rule", "label": "Two-adapters rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One adapter means a hypothetical seam; two adapters means a real one - don't cut a seam until something actually varies across it."}, {"id": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_feathers", "label": "Michael Feathers (seam term)", "file_type": "paper", "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": "Michael Feathers", "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_deep_module", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_seam", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_deletion_test", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_two_adapters_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_seam", "target": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_feathers", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_domain_modeling_domain_modeling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_tdd_tdd", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_improve_codebase_architecture_improve_codebase_architecture", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "readme_to_spec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_codebase_design", "target": "docs_engineering_ask_matt_ask_matt", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "skills/skills/docs/engineering/codebase-design.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_engineering_codebase_design_deletion_test", "target": "docs_engineering_improve_codebase_architecture_dele